Status: Pending. Owner refinement, 2026-11-14: explore through the things in the workspace, inspired by Everything. Planning approval is not implementation evidence.

[Development graph](../Workspace-Development.lingua) · [Exploration contracts](../contracts/Exploration-contracts.lingua)

## Start gate

Required completed export: [Local navigation](Navigation.lingua), including its inherited frame, selection, asset, query and input contracts.

This branch delivers observation and traversal on supplied local objects. It may proceed alongside geometry authoring after navigation is verified. Moving an object through possession is owned by [Possession](Possession.lingua), which also waits for functional behavior services. Globe data, imported splats, character rigs, PCB authoring and numerical simulation are not prerequisites for this branch.

## Delivered boundary

Select an object or assembly, adopt its viewpoint or reference frame, follow it, enter available internal structure, move outward and return to the previous context. The same operations work on supported subjects at different scales without changing their physical dimensions, model fidelity or accepted state. Observation does not grant control.

## Ownership and possible overlap

Own the exploration session, native navigation actions and bounded history over the existing view service. Reuse occurrence identity, source correspondence, input/focus, asset demand and permissions. Coordinate changes to shared view/frame schemas with their owner in the current checkout; independent leaf work may overlap, shared service edits have one owner. Possession and optional automatic exploration consume this verified export without inventing another camera or scene system.

## Ordered work

### Task EXP.T01

- [ ] Freeze EXP.F01 and the shared context descriptor: selected occurrence and source revision; document/view root; display frame and units; viewpoint anchor and explicit local axes/up; camera/pivot and projection; observation/follow mode; selected clock; tool/focus state; entry relation and return context. Reuse existing fields and bounded view-state storage. Distinguish source containment, an explicitly linked model and a representative specimen. The session may observe an object with no locomotion profile, rig or physical body.

### Task EXP.T02

- [ ] Add native Observe/Follow actions to ordinary selection and the accessible object list. Use an authored viewpoint when supplied and an inspectable bounds-based observation anchor otherwise; never infer eyes or a locomotion direction from a name. Keep world-relative and object-relative orientation explicit. Follow a changing source transform without changing it, preserve a useful camera distance at the subject's scale, and support an immediate exit to the previous view. A sensor image uses its real supported image binding when available; looking from an anchor does not invent sensor output.

### Task EXP.T03

- [ ] Add Enter, Surroundings and Back with a readable current subject/path. Enter selects available internals or an explicitly linked view; it does not synthesize missing anatomy, atoms, buildings or containing worlds. Surroundings follows the chosen occurrence context; Back follows the actual entry history, which may differ in a reused assembly. Preserve view/focus intent through source correspondence, unit changes and origin shifts. Restore the saved context when still valid; if the subject moved, restore its declared relative view, and if it was deleted or access was lost, retain a valid permitted context with a visible explanation. Bound history and release inactive payload leases rather than retaining every visited detail.

### Task EXP.T04

- [ ] Integrate pointer/keyboard operation, readable status, movement preferences and reduced-motion/immediate transitions through the existing controls. Keep physical placement, display magnification, navigation speed, selected time and behavior model independent. Cancel or complete active edits through their existing protocol before changing context; never silently accept a half-finished edit. Missing, private or offline detail retains the last usable view and provides a discoverable return action. Use the existing inspector and preserve the edit-panel geometry requirement in [Lince](../../../Lince.lingua), including the visible bottom-left controls.

### Task EXP.T05

- [ ] Prove EXP.W01 and EXP.W02 through native actions, source/permission failure injection and the bounded fixture. Cover a noncharacter object, a moving reference frame, reused occurrences with different parents, a linked representative sample and a root with no outer world. Record context accuracy, transition responsiveness, active/retained bytes, source requests and last-demand release. Publish the session/input handoff before possession or automatic exploration starts; their absence does not delay this export.

## Completion and handoff

Publish actual view/session ownership, supported entry relations, persisted preferences versus temporary history, context repair behavior, adopted workload/resource limits and native proof links. Require zero accepted model mutations, physical rescaling, implicit solver starts or control grants from observation/traversal. Keep EXP.W01/EXP.W02 evidence pending until the real workflow passes.

Consumers: [Possession](Possession.lingua), [optional automatic exploration](Automatic-Exploration.lingua) and [exploration acceptance](../contracts/Exploration-contracts.lingua). Full core acceptance consumes the composed exploration contract. Current outcome: unbuilt and unverified.
